    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Check NWS updates here At 925 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking showers and thunderstorms with strong wind gusts along the Northern Rocky Mountain Front and the high plains west of interstate 15. Movement was east at 35 mph. HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph. SOURCE...Radar indicated. IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured objects. Locations impacted include... Shelby, Cut Bank, Conrad, Choteau, Browning, Valier, Sunburst, Kevin, Heart Butte, East Glacier Park Village, North Browning, Kiowa, South Browning, East Glacier Park, Sweet Grass, Dupuyer, Oilmont, Santa Rita, Ferdig, and Ethridge.",
